<article class="enc-article">
<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Višeslav of Serbia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. c. 780</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Višeslav is the earliest Serbian ruler known by name, recorded by the Byzantine emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantine-vii">Constantine VII</a> Porphyrogennetos as a descendant of the leader who brought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbs">Serbs</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkans">Balkans</a>. He is usually dated to around 780 and is regarded as the founder of the Vlastimirović dynasty, though nothing more is known of his rule.</p></div>
